# Park phone-call dialogue.
# Format: see data/dialogue/school.dlg. One line = one page (click to advance).
# Placeholders {place} {player_name} are filled in by ParkCall.gd via
# Dialogue.get_pages(..., fmt).
#
# Plays once, on the walk home from the first school or work run, after the
# work-disruption call where the player stole the robot chest, on which the
# player steals something (nanobots or scrap) - see Main._maybe_show_park_call. She calls,
# admits she can still track the player's phone, warns that patrol drones route
# through the park, and pushes the player to connect the chest to her head.
# The patrol-drone encounter can't happen until this call has played (see
# Main._maybe_show_post_activity_drone_encounter).
#
# Plays: [call] + ([chest.unattached] or [chest.attached]) + [closing].
# The line containing "buzzes" loops the ringtone (ParkCall.PHONE_RING_CUE).
# The line containing "up at the sky" cuts to park_sky (the bird, phone hidden),
# and the next line cuts back to the park with the phone back up
# (ParkCall.PARK_SKY_CUE). Keep that phrase if you reword it.

[call]
[i]You cut through the park on the walk home from {place}. It's quiet out here.[/i]
Your phone buzzes in your pocket. Unknown number again.
You answer the call.
You: …Hello?
Her: I hope you're enjoying your little walk through the park.
You: What? How do you know where I am? I turned my GPS off.
You double-check and confirm that your location is still hidden.
Her: You turned the GPS off. Not the phone.
Her: I can still find you through it. Cell towers, wifi.
Her: You were easier to find than I thought you'd be.
Thoughts: That's comforting...
You: Should I hang up?
Her: That'd only make tracking you slightly harder. 
Her: Plus, as far as I know, a phone call isn't illegal.
You: You'd be surprised what's illegal nowadays.
Her: I can see the patrol drones' routes from here. A few of them pass right through this park.
[i]You glance up at the sky above the trees. Nothing yet, just a bird.[/i]
Her: So watch out for them around here in the mornings. [color=#df7f7f]Especially when you're carrying something you shouldn't be.[/color]
You: Good thing I'm not carrying anything illegal...
Her: Right.

[chest.unattached]
Her: Hey listen… you still haven't attached me to the chest you stole...
You: I've been a little busy, you know. Getting you parts, not getting arrested.
Her: There's an app on your laptop that can help connect the chest to my head.
Her: It'll do the hard part for you.
You: Why the rush?
Her: Do you know what it's like being just a head?
She raises her voice.
Her: So-rry, Mr. Head-and-shoulders! Forgive me for wanting a body!
You:...
Her: It's uncomfortable. All the time. Being stuck in this stupid backpack.
Thoughts: I never really thought about it like that.
Her: A chest is a start. Please, {player_name}.
You: …I'll see what I can do.

[chest.attached]
Her: Get home soon.

[closing]
[i]She hangs up before you can say anything else.[/i]
Thoughts: I'm risking a lot for her...